ess. With Queen-high (no pair), I have a very weak hand that loses to any pair. However, since I can check for free, folding would be wasteful. Betting would be too risky with essentially nothing - if they call with any pair, I lose. The most prudent play is to check and see if my Queen-high is somehow good enough, though I expect to lose most of the time. This minimizes losses on a hand where I have very little equity.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
