d. A bluff is also risky because the opponent has shown they're willing to see showdown.\n\nReason:\n\nWith only a pair of 7s on a board showing A-K-7-4-3, my hand is quite weak. My opponent has checked through every street, suggesting they also have a marginal hand. However, betting here would be risky because any Ace, King, or higher pair beats me, and my opponent would likely call with those hands. Since I can check for free and see the showdown, there's no reason to risk chips. The pot is small anyway (just blinds), so there's minimal value to extract even if I'm ahead.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
