rong hand either. However, with three Aces on board, anyone with a kicker higher than 9 beats me, and that's statistically very likely. A raise here would be a bluff that only makes sense if I think my opponent has absolute garbage (both cards lower than 9). Since I'm already losing overall and this is a marginal spot at best, checking to showdown is the safest play. There's a small pot to win, and checking costs me nothing.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
